			"SHA": "c49dff70aa6c2683d4d207a8a91c749c015e6c3e"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-22T05:33:48Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				149,
				6
			],
			"Message": "feat(Sky): Integrate VS Code workbench services into bridge handlers\n\nThe bridge handlers in InstallEditorAndOutput, InstallUiRequests, InstallScm, InstallSimpleRelays, InstallEditorOperations, and Notification were stubs or DOM-only fallbacks that prevented extensions from receiving proper UI feedback and text editing.\n\nImplement WorkspaceEdit (applyEdit) via IBulkEditService or direct Monaco text model operations, normalise extHostTypes.WorkspaceEdit serialization format, and handle file create/rename/delete via Mountain IPC. Add save/saveAll/saveAs round-trip handlers. Wire INotificationService for toasts with clickable action buttons that resolve the Mountain oneshot, and IQuickInputService for native input boxes and quick-pick widgets with keyboard navigation and fuzzy matching. Add retry logic for SCM provider registration to handle workbench service initialisation race. Call Monaco's setLanguageConfiguration directly for bracket-matching and auto-indent. Extract range conversion helpers (ExtL, ExtC) for both VS Code 0-based and Monaco 1-based ranges. Add OnAction callback to ShowNotification for DOM toast round-trip resolution with auto-dismiss null fallback.\n\nExtensions now get VS Code-native dialogs, text editing, and UI prompts through the workbench service layer instead of DOM fallbacks.",
			"SHA": "779146fbca3a7bdfb7be1285ef792fe6908f6c23"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-22T03:01:35Z",
